				732,
				48
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Split WindServiceHandlers and CocoonService into atomic domain modules\n\nRefactor the IPC layer by splitting monolithic handlers into focused domain modules:\n\n**WindServiceHandler split (24 modules):**\n- Command, Configuration, Decoration, Environment, Extension, FileSystem\n- History, Keybinding, Label, Lifecycle, Model, NativeHost\n- Notification, Output, Progress, QuickInput, Search, Storage\n- Terminal, TextFile, Theme, WorkingCopy, Workspace\n- Each module contains handlers for its domain with proper error handling\n\n**CocoonService split (15 modules):**\n- Auth, Command, Debug, Extension, FileSystem, Output, Provider\n- SCM, Save, Secret, Task, Terminal, TreeView, Window, Workspace\n- Language feature provider handlers consolidated in Provider.rs\n\n**Additional changes:**\n- Fix MutexGuard scope in FeatureMethods.rs (lock held across await point)\n- Remove duplicate dev_log imports in AdvancedFeatures.rs and WindAdvancedSync.rs\n- Simplify TraceLog.rs and ConfigurationInitialize.rs (remove excess docs)\n- Add comprehensive CHANGELOG.md documenting v0.0 through v2.1\n- Update mod.rs to re-export helper functions for submodules\n\nThis modular structure improves maintainability and enables parallel development of domain-specific IPC handlers.",
			"SHA": "f8dd70ea95583cfeee8936cc7eb8b022b141465f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-16T12:48:36Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				691,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Fix command registration locking and provider registration path\n\nCorrect the registerCommand handler to properly lock the CommandRegistry before insertion and use the correct CommandHandler::Proxied structure with SideCarIdentifier and CommandIdentifier fields. Also fix the provider registration handler to use self.RunTime.Environment instead of self.Environment for proper runtime state access.\n\nThese changes ensure commands from Cocoon extensions are correctly registered in the command registry and provider registrations flow to the correct runtime state.",
			"SHA": "4945b47bbc5f6dc146e5d6f625ba0394ddf837d7"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-16T12:44:52Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				691,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Mountain): Add json macro import to MountainVinegRPCService\n\nAdd serde_json::json macro to imports in MountainVinegRPCService to enable JSON construction for gRPC message handling. This supports building structured JSON payloads for the Vine protocol service layer.",
			"SHA": "a2ef2b5714239e43f8f9b3e95dceff8922f4ffcb"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-16T12:44:26Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				691,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Handle extension registration notifications from Cocoon\n\nAdd three new notification handlers in MountainVinegRPCService to process messages from the Cocoon extension host:\n\n1. **window.showMessage**: Forward info/warn/error messages from extensions to the Sky UI layer via `sky://notification/show` Tauri event\n\n2. **registerCommand**: Store proxied extension commands in CommandRegistry with \"cocoon-main\" sidecar identifier, enabling Wind to route command execution back to Cocoon\n\n3. **Provider registration fallback**: Handle provider registration via the vscode API shim path (register_hover_provider, register_completion_item_provider, etc.) as a fallback for providers registered outside the typed RPC path\n\nThese handlers enable proper bidirectional communication between extensions running in Cocoon and the Mountain/Sky layers, completing the extension registration flow initiated in the recent LanguageFeatureProviderRegistry commits.",
			"SHA": "0bcd60d909e8c6a367c440e5ecf89140ce0f8303"
		}
